---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About">
  <main class="container">
    <article class="page prose">
      <header class="hero text-center">
        <img
          src="/images/profile.jpg"
          alt="Gabriel"
          width="160"
          height="160"
          class="rounded-full mx-auto mb-8 object-cover border-4 border-[var(--border-strong)]"
        />
        <h1>About</h1>
      </header>

      <p>Hi, I'm Gabriel — a slow learner trying to build things on the internet in 2026.</p>

      <p>
        I live in Cebu City, Philippines. I used to think I needed to rush through bootcamps and tutorials
        to "catch up". Turns out that approach just made me anxious and forgetful.
      </p>

      <p>
        So now I'm doing it differently:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>One tool at a time (currently Astro + vanilla CSS)</li>
        <li>Writing what I learn instead of just consuming</li>
        <li>Building in public, even when it's messy</li>
        <li>No daily streaks, no pressure metrics — just steady curiosity</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        This site is my notebook. It's not meant to be impressive. It's meant to be honest.
      </p>

      <p>
        If you're also learning slowly, feel free to stay. You're not behind — you're just on a different rhythm.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-12 text-center text-[var(--text-muted)]">
        Say hello → <a href="https://x.com/Enoch" class="text-[var(--accent)] hover:underline">@Enoch</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose ul {
    list-style: disc;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 1.5rem 1.5rem;
  }
  .prose li {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
</style>
